      "details": "Locked target and manifest are pinned; current flash materializations are pinned and their SHA-256 values match the ledger entries. Main image load base 0x438000 and bootloader base 0x410000 agree with active image materialization mapping; main wrapped-vs-stripped coordinate distinction was retained."
    },
    "table_offsets_and_bytes": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "For each image, runtime table start minus load base equals the ledger image offset. Direct little-endian unpack of 24 bytes confirms exactly one dispatch word, two (size,destination) pairs, and zero sentinel. Table-byte SHA-256 matches."
    },
    "generated_zero_spans": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "For all four records, independently recomputed size and destination + size exactly match span endpoints; SHA-256(bytes(size)) matches generated_zero_sha256. These are deterministic RAM zero bytes."
    },
    "nested_image_distinction": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "The four outputs describe zero-filled destination RAM intervals only. Encoded nested/compressed images are separate flash source spans and are not included in these zero-byte hashes or claimed as decoded outputs."
    },
    "historical_cross_check": {
      "status": "consistent_with_distilled_reference",
      "details": "The consolidated Apollo platform reference documents main zero-init rows 0x70AF0 -> 0x20004558 and 0x240FD4 -> 0x2013BE70, absolute destinations, and zero-init handler flag convention. Current review independently confirms these main rows from current materialized image bytes. Bootloader records were checked directly from current bootloader bytes; historical replay receipts are pinned only as contextual references, not treated as proof."
    }
